r['interpretation']+=(' Q4 (opacity and shock tracers): the H13CN 4-3 limits (HCN/H13CN >8 at N and S, >5 Bridge) bound tau(HCN 4-3) only if Tex are equal (<4-12), and RADEX shows they exclude none of the ladder-allowed solutions, so HCN opacity is NOT measured by H13CN; the ladder solutions have tau(HCN 3-2) of order 10-40 (thick), but the data cannot fix N(HCN). At 0.24" the peak Tb ratio HCN/HCO+ is 0.93 at N (consistent with both thick) and 0.46 at S (HCN thin-ish if HCO+ is thick). No IR pumping (v2=1f/v=0 <3-9%). SO is cold/sub-thermal (Trot<=12 K in the 9x6" beam), CH3OH and SiS appear only in extended gas at the Bridge/S-extension/Soutflow in 6" beams and not at the nuclei (<0.013/<0.017 of HCO+); the Band-5 CH3OH Q-branch excess of 1.5-2x is not a maser signature (no inversion in RADEX, normal profile) and is consistent with cold extended CH3OH if Xb4f resolves out half the flux. S being HCO+-bright rather than HCN-faint is favoured by CS and H2CS also being weak relative to HCO+ at S, but HCN under-abundance vs HCO+ enhancement is not separable with these data.')
r['caveats']+=['Q4: H13CN is on the red wing of CO 3-2 (core out of band); detection at N (alpha 0.03-0.075) depends on the wing model; a limit is quoted. The equal-Tex tau bound is invalid in sub-thermal gas (RADEX): the earlier Q1b "tau43<=5.5" shortcut should be read with this caveat.',
 'Q4: HCN v2=1f limits assume equal beam filling and thin vib line; IR pumping in a source much smaller than 47 pc would be diluted in all beams. SO 4_5-3_4 flux changed from 1.25 Jy/beam km/s (peak pixel, no wing subtraction) to 0.63+-0.08 K km/s (=0.97 Jy/beam km/s at 9.4x6.3") after fitting the HCO+ wing; Band-5 SO is blended N+S+Bridge. CH3OH maser test depends on the unknown flux recovery of Xb4f relative to Band 5; the 6_5-5_4 SO temperature limit scales the same way. HOC+ and HC15N hints are 3-3.5 sigma only. To settle: HCO+/H13CO+ or HC18O+ (not in band), matched 1-0 lines, and short-spacing Band 6 data.']
json.dump(r,open(P,'w'),indent=1)
